@MihaZupan and @karelz sorry I missed the notification on the original reply.

The `QueryHelper` proposal looks useful and sounds like it could work for us in general terms. We essentially have two `NameValueCollection`s which we combine and then format a final query string value from them. My only concern would be the [comment](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/32606#issuecomment-589897073) which suggests that API would focus more on general usability rather than low allocations. 

Our approach can certainly be further optimised and I feel the above API would still be useful in more advanced cases. It would be interesting to compare its performance against `QueryBuilder` if that is also approved.

